==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Greater Demon Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Greater Balrog Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Lesser Demon Cat has single target attacks and short range. In exchange for these weaknesses, he deals devastating damage to a single target. To prevent this from being too big a problem, he should be paired with [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]], [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attack]] or just [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attack]] Cats (such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]]) to wipe out obstructive peons. Even then, however, it is important to understand that he is not meant for stages that spam enemies, and is more suitable for stages with more durable entities, preferably with the support of other crowd-controllers. One such example is [[Primitive Souls]], where he can easily neutralize [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]] after the [[Dark Otter]]s are taken out. He can also take on said Dark Otters, melting nasty peons like butter when your other units just can't cut it, but unless there are other exploitable attributes, Lesser Demon Cat will struggle a lot against enemies that outrange him.

Additionally, Lesser Demon Cat has a quick cooldown and relatively low cost, making him incredibly disposable even compared to the likes of [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. On another note, this unit is Immune to Weaken, allowing him to be more effective when the few enemies with this ability, like [[Cli-One]] and [[Calamary]], are on the field. Notably, if the way is clear, Lesser Demon Cat can possibly tank a [[Hannya]] hit to the face and then dish out his full devastation, able to destroy Hannya before yet another attack.

As a unit heavily reliant on stats, you should put a significant investment in his levels. This gives him more damage and more health, which can make all the difference he has on the field.

Lesser Demon also has two [[Cat Combo]]s, [[Speak of the Devil (Combo)|Speak Of The Devil]] and [[Lust for Battle (Combo)|Lust for Battle]]. Speak Of The Devil increases Accounting Power (the money gained from enemies) and thus can be very helpful in [[:Category:Li'l Stages|Li'l Stages]] and otherwise 4-crown [[Stories of Legend]]. Lust For Battle is almost completely outclassed by [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]]/[[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]], [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]], or [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]] in normal circumstances, however if you were going to use [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] anyways, it's not the worst option available.

==='''True Form'''===
The transition from Greater Demon Cat to Greater Balrog Cat gives no new abilities, but improves his health and attack power considerably. This change is enough solidify him as an absolutely phenomenal source of frontline offense, especially when boosted to high levels. A combination of extremely high stats and incredibly low cost and cooldown makes Balrog an incredibly valuable unit in endgame. Balrog's cost for his damage means that, oftentimes, getting only one hit off on the main target is enough for Balrog to be worth his cost. If he stays around for long enough, he can proceed to deal massive amounts of DPS, greatly crippling if not outright killing the main threat of the stage. True Form also grants him access to talents, further augmenting his destructive potential. It should be noted, however, that he requires a large talent investment to reach his full potential, arguably more so than any other uber.

==='''Talents'''===
His most important [[Talents|Talent]] is Strengthen, which can greatly increase his DPS if he lands enough hits on his final knockback. Balrog's Strengthen is no joke, getting 200% more damage. Fundamentally tripling his AP, consequently gives him some of the highest DPS in the game at any level of investment. However, this damage boost matters little if he isn't able to stay on the field long enough to make them count. Health Up can help with that, allowing safer use in general, and Attack Up can boost his already high damage even further, to the point where he does the most DPS in the game. Balrog's Strengthen is currently one of the highest priority across all Uber talents in the game; with his already high stats, the basic stat boosts are also more valuable than what they seem.

Cost Down is another very strong Talent, though it dulls in priority compared to the stat boosts. The usual 3000¢ for Balrog is already a great deal compared to most other Uber Rare Cats, but lowering that to 2250¢ allows for one to summon him incredibly early and makes a spam of Balrogs possible with cash to spare in most stages.

Although Wave Resist makes Balrog a lot more viable against certain dangerous wave threats, these situations either necessitate the use of a Wave Shield, or preclude the possibility of using Balrog entirely due to the availability of other, more consistent units. It therefore ends up being a huge investment for not much gain.

==='''Orb'''===
Effect orbs won't be much use on Greater Balrog since they will only increase effectiveness against a single trait. Ability orbs, on the other hand, can give Balrog great buffs. Stories of Legend buff won't be much use on Balrog, although to be fair those orbs aren't much use in general. An S-tier Resist Wave orb combined with the Talent will give Balrog full immunity, although once again that's not much use for Balrog specifically.

Colossus Slayer can be of great use, but it's nowhere near as useful as Death Mini-Surge or Cash Back. Death Mini-Surge can deal a massive amount of damage to enemies after death, and it has both piercing range and area attack, covering Balrog's main offensive weaknesses. However, obtaining an S-Rank Death Mini-Surge Orb would require playing [[Ranking Dojo|Arena of Destiny]] 3 times for a chance at dealing at most 86,400 damage every second Balrog, and this hit can easily miss due random surge appearance. Cash Back can save a lot of money, especially for a unit with Balrog's cooldown, although with Balrog's cost down talent he's already quite cheap. Shortened Cooldown Orb can be used with research Cat Combos for spam up to 1/3 faster for every 2nd Balrog.

