==Trivia==
*Although Lesser Demon Cat was added in Version 2.0, it was inaccessible until [[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.5 Update|Version 2.0.5]] fully implemented THE DYNAMITES set.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Lesser Demon Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Dynamites (Removed Combo)|Dynamites]].
*Prior to [[Version 5.3 Update|Version 5.3]], where he became [[Immune to Weaken]], Lesser Demon Cat used to be one of the few [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] that lacked an ability.
*Prior to [[Version 10.1 Update|Version 10.1]] of [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Lesser Demon Cat's true form name was "Balrog Cat". It was changed most likely to prevent confusion with [[Balrog Cat (Rare Cat)|Balrog Cat]] from the [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event|Street Fighter]] Collab, and other units named [[Balrog (disambiguation)|Balrog]].
*Prior to [[Version 10.4 Update|Version 10.4]] of [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], Greater Demon Cat had a typo in his description: "The mad cat managed to control '''the a''' demon from the netherworld. Attacks with extreme force."
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Lesser Demon Cat's description had a typo: "...that sacrificed itself to '''a a''' demon..."
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Lesser Demon Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Lesser Demon Cat
A mad cat that sacrificed itself to
a demon from the netherworld.
Attacks with extreme force.</pre>
<pre>Greater Demon Cat
The mad cat managed to control
the demon from the netherworld.
Attacks with extreme force.</pre>
<pre>Greater Balrog Cat
His wanderings through the abyss have
driven him mad with infernal ambitions.
Tremendous damage to a single enemy.</pre>
*According to his Japanese name and description, Lesser Demon Cat is specifically an ''[[wikipedia:Oni|Oni]]'', a demon-like yōkai with a Kanabo as a weapon and two horns on its head.
*Greater Demon Cat's description contains the word "slake", meaning to quench or satisfy a desire.
*Balrog could be a reference to the fiery demon in ''The Lord of the Rings''. Gandalf the Grey fought and defeated the Balrog in the abyss which lead to his ascension as Gandalf the White.
*When Lesser Demon Cat moves, he doesn't actually stay still, instead his sprite moves backwards to make it seem like he is still. This is more noticeable when he is slowed or has any other effect, The same is true for [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]].
*As of Version 15.7, Lesser Demon Cat is the oldest Uber from the main [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] banners to not have an [[Ultra Form]] or [[Ultra Talents]].

